                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Game won't load in solo or otherwise. Not sure if this is an Australia-specific issue but USD$15 seems too much for a loading screen and a settings page.\n\n21/01/2018 - Tried again this morning and still unable to play. The game reports that there are 2 players in my region and I appear to be stuck waiting for at least 15 players before the game can begin.\n\n21/01/2018 - Tried a third time this evening. If you click the public (green) button before hitting the start button, you can launch a solo game. Doesn't seem to work if you hit start before toggling the public setting. And. Wow. I actually had a higher opinion of the game when I was stuck on the loading screen. If you climb to the top of a hill and look out at the horizon, you see... nothing. There is a thick \"fog\" that prevents you from seeing anything further than your immediate surroundings. Shortly after descending the hill I was attacked by a zombie that took 2 swings at me and then disappeared. Walking further into the fog I eventually found 2 houses which contained several items that were scattered across the floors at even intervals as if the house floor was built out of very large squares of floor that could only hold 1 item. Some of the items were consumable but didn't seem to have any real purpose. At this point, the game is more like a tech demo than an actual game.",
